> > There might be some eastern myth of privileged people changing into a
> > whole new adult body[1], but in the western re-incarnation schools,
> > having to go through the troubles of being born is part of the severe
> > punishment physical existence and re-incarnation represent.
> 
> There's no need to follow one myth above the other.

Sure. Just an example of real-world reincarnation beliefs; as i
understand it, buddhism and hinduism also consider the cycle of
reincarnation a continuation of suffering and an undesirable form of
existence.

As far as the idea is concerned, the main question for me is: does it
add something interesting to the game? - not really, it's just another
sort of life saving. Could be interesting to replace "proper" life
saving with it; i really like your idea of renaming the amulet of life
saving to amulet of reincarnation for some classes.

The idea of re-incarnation as we find it in real-world beliefs doesn't
exactly lend itself to NetHack implementation. Trying to fiddle with
it to make it implementable is only worth it if it can add something
substantial to the game - or if it makes for a working replacement of
the amulet of life saving. I have some troubles with the name, but i'm
probably over-scrupulous as far as mythological correctness is
concerned.

